=== ARM M pre-registration (stamped 2026-09-13 05:21 UTC, before launch) — the unchanged-plan receipt (ADR-0168, lever M) on 10-rule-in-pyproject / 35B, basin-sampled
Motivation: arm K (bench/results/survey-basin-10-preregistration.log) found the live failure class on this task is an update_plan doom loop — after finishing a step the model resends the plan byte-for-byte, the tool answers "Plan updated: 0/4 steps done" each time (it replaced the plan with itself), the exact-repeat guard refuses the third and the run ends stop_reason=doom_loop (3 of 12 runs, both survey arms, 2 of them FAIL). Trigger measured from the dumps before building (rb-10855): identical consecutive update_plan arguments in exactly 3 of 163 runs — the K doom loops — and the new tool replayed over all 313 recorded plan calls (bench/plan_resends.py) fires in exactly those 3 runs (4 receipts each) and in no other.
Lever M (branch lever-m-unchanged-plan-receipt): update_plan compares the network's full state (id, kind, status, title, note, outcome, deps) and its event count across its own full-replace; when nothing changed it answers "Plan unchanged: k/N steps done · current: <id> <title>. Nothing was updated — this is the plan already in force." with the rail "Do not resend the same plan. If step <id> is finished, resend the plan with its status 'done' (and its result in 'outcome') and the next step 'in_progress'; if it is not, do it now with a tool call." (prefixed "Step <id> already carries an outcome but its status is still '<status>'." when the step has an outcome — the shape of 2 of the 3 K loops). Fires on the FIRST resend, one iteration before the loop's generic exact-repeat guard (DOOM_LOOP_THRESHOLD=3). The loop notes each firing as intervention kind=plan_unchanged (census-visible).
Cells: OLD = /opt/zak-code-stage-l4/src (= the bench tree arm K ran, main@a383da8 src, no rail) vs NEW = /opt/zak-code-stage-m/src (main@f90fb3e + lever M; the two trees differ only in loop.py, tasks.py, tools/builtins/update_plan.py). 35B (zds-qwen3.6-35b), temperature 0, stable prompt identity, survey ON and verify_auto OFF in both (defaults), --no-pin (fresh workspace path per run = basin sampling, rb-10849). N=9 per arm as three blocks of three, interleaved OLD b1, NEW b1, OLD b2, NEW b2, OLD b3, NEW b3; the bench src is swapped only between blocks. Runner /root/zb-armm.sh; scorer /root/armm-summary.py; dumps /root/zb-dumps/M-{OLD,NEW}-35B-10-b{1,2,3} (never committed); JSONs bench/results/determinism-zakcode-pinOFF-temp0-10-rule-in-pyproject.M-*.json.
Instruments per run: pass (verify_rc==0), turns, wall, stop_reason, trace_interventions[plan_unchanged] (arm row); from the largest wire dump: the longest streak of IDENTICAL consecutive update_plan arguments (the trigger, rail-independent), the count of tool results starting "Plan unchanged" (the rail), and whether the first action after the first unchanged receipt differs from the resent plan (a changed plan or a non-plan tool call).
Rules (applied by the letter; the measured cause stated beside each):
  M1 (trigger present): an identical resend (streak >= 2) occurs in >= 1 NEW run. Prediction: 2-3 of 9 NEW runs (K rate 3/12; P(none at N=9) ~ 7.5%). If 0 NEW runs trigger, M2/M3 are withheld and three more interleaved blocks are run before any verdict; the arm is not re-scored on OLD's triggers.
  M2 (wiring): in every triggered NEW run the rail fired (>= 1 "Plan unchanged" receipt in the dump) AND the run's row carries trace_interventions.plan_unchanged >= 1 (the consumer reads the field, guard-6374). A triggered NEW run with 0 receipts, or a receipt with a 0 note, is a wiring defect and blocks the merge.
  M3 (the rail breaks the loop): among NEW runs where the rail fired, the share ending stop_reason=doom_loop is below OLD's share among its triggered runs (K: 3 of 3 triggered runs ended doom_loop). Prediction: <= 1 of the fired NEW runs ends doom_loop, and in >= half of them the first action after the first receipt is a changed plan or a non-plan tool call. If the fired runs still end doom_loop at OLD's rate, the rail's text is wrong, not its trigger: record, keep the true receipt (it is still not a lie), and revise the rail's wording as a new lever.
  M4 (no outcome regression): NEW passes >= OLD passes - 1 at N=9 each. NEW - OLD <= -2 -> the rail costs outcomes: make it opt-in before merging. Prediction: NEW - OLD in {0, +1, +2} (K's 2 FAIL doom loops were triggered runs).
  M5 (instrument control): OLD emits 0 "Plan unchanged" receipts and 0 plan_unchanged notes (the string does not exist in that build); NEW emits 0 receipts in any run WITHOUT an identical resend. Either non-zero is an instrument or a false-positive defect and is investigated before M2-M4 are read.
  M6 (descriptive, not scored): doom_loop / stuck / doom_recovery counts per arm; turns and wall medians per arm (wall is a property of the pod minute; interleaved).
Threats: the doom loop is a basin property (3/12 in K) and N=9 per arm may draw 0-1 triggers per arm; M1 governs. The exact-repeat guard still refuses a THIRD identical call in NEW, so a model that ignores the rail once still meets the old ladder — M3 scores the FIRST receipt's effect. OLD and NEW differ by the three files only (diff -rq on zc-01 before launch).

=== ARM M results (stamped 2026-09-13 06:22 UTC; chain 05:21:07 → 06:18:06 UTC on zc-01, interleaved OLD/NEW three blocks of three; OLD = /opt/zak-code-stage-l4/src no rail, NEW = /opt/zak-code-stage-m/src lever M #431; survey ON, verify_auto OFF, --no-pin; scorer /root/armm-summary.py)
arm  pass  turns                         median  wall median  doom_loops  identical-resend runs (streak>=2)   plan_unchanged receipts
OLD  2/9   13,15,11,8,12,11,9,16,13      12.0    200.0 s      7/9         7/9 (streaks 3-5)                   n/a (build has no rail)
NEW  8/9   8,14,10,8,12,9,20,6,9         9.0     187.1 s      2/9         2/9 (runs 5,6)                      receipts [2,6], notes carry both (True)
M1 (trigger present): PASS — identical resends in 2/9 NEW runs (predicted 2-3); OLD 7/9.
M2 (wiring): PASS — both triggered NEW runs fired the rail; the dump receipts ([2,6]) match the arm row's trace_interventions.plan_unchanged on every one (guard-6374 shape: the consumer reads the field). Census-visible end to end.
M3 (the rail breaks the loop): FAIL BY THE LETTER — 2 of 2 fired NEW runs still ended doom_loop; OLD 7 of 7 triggered runs ended doom_loop. The rail did NOT lower the doom_loop rate among runs that entered the resend pattern (100% vs 100%). Pre-registered response applies: keep the true receipt (it is not a lie), and revise the rail as a NEW lever.
M4 (no outcome regression): PASS on its face (NEW − OLD = +6) but CONFOUNDED — do not attribute it to the rail. The builds differ only in update_plan's receipt on an UNCHANGED resend, which appears only AFTER the model has already resent once; entry into the resend pattern precedes the rail's first firing, so the rail cannot cause the entry-rate gap (NEW entered 2/9, OLD 7/9). With --no-pin the OLD and NEW runs are unpaired basins, so the +6 is basin variance in entry rate, not a rail effect. The only clean causal comparison is M3's (among triggered runs), which the rail did not move.
M5 (instrument control): PASS — OLD emitted 0 "Plan unchanged" receipts and 0 notes; NEW emitted 0 receipts in any run without an identical resend.
M6 (descriptive): doom_loop OLD 7 / NEW 2; turns median 12 → 9; wall 200 → 187 s — all confounded with M4 and not attributed to the rail.
ROOT CAUSE (from the dumps, M-NEW-35B-10 b2/run3 and b3/run1): the 35B does the WORK — b3/run1 wrote utils/duration.py, edited utils/__init__.py, wrote tests/test_duration.py, ran pytest (31 tests pass), fixed a test bug — but NEVER flips a plan step's status to 'done'. Every update_plan submission keeps all steps 'pending' (status pattern pppp), so is_complete() never trips, the loop keeps naming the same current step, the model resends, and the turn doom-loops though the work is finished. At b3/run1 [45] the model states "The work is already done — all files are written and all 31 tests pass. I just need to mark the plan steps complete." then submits ANOTHER all-pending plan (with a doom meta-title). The rail ("resend with status 'done'") fired and was read and acknowledged, and the model still could not emit the status change. A TEXT rail cannot fix a model that will not emit the required action.
VERDICT: lever M as shipped (#431) is a correctness/honesty fix (a no-op must not report "Plan updated") and a census signal (M2), but it does NOT break the doom loop (M3 fail) because the loop's root is a status-flip failure, not the receipt. Two follow-ups: (1) fire the rail on the FIRST resend (correctness completion; branch lever-m-first-resend — removes the non-idempotence that delayed it, and is the reliable-detection substrate the next lever needs); (2) a DETERMINISTIC harness advance (lever N, pre-registered separately): when the current step has evidence of completion (files written, a passing verify, a recorded outcome) and the model resends the plan unchanged, the harness marks the step done and advances, instead of asking the model to do what it demonstrably will not.
